145:Three of the five features were represented directly by baseline input variables ($E_\mathrm{lipid}$, $f_\mathrm{calc}$, and $\theta_\mathrm{lipid}$). The remaining two, plaque burden ($PB$) and functional gradient ($\Delta\mathrm{FFR}$), were not input variables but were instead derived from the geometry and simulation results. Plaque burden was evaluated at the minimum-lumen-area (MLA) cross-section, defined as the plane at which the lumen diameter was smallest. It was computed in the conventional cross-sectional form as $PB = (A_\mathrm{vessel} - A_\mathrm{lumen})/A_\mathrm{vessel} \times 100\%$, where $A_\mathrm{vessel}$ and $A_\mathrm{lumen}$ are the vessel-wall-bounded and luminal areas on that plane~\cite{mintz2001ivus}. $\Delta\mathrm{FFR}$ was computed as $FFR_\mathrm{prox} - FFR_\mathrm{dist} = 1 - P_d/P_\mathrm{in}$, with the distal pressure $P_d$ taken as the cross-sectional mean $3\,\mathrm{cm}$ downstream of the lesion~\cite{lee2019emerald, cami2018ffrct}.

